你是一个数学答案验证系统，请判断以下数学问题的答案是否正确：

问题：What is the ratio of the volume of cone $A$ to the volume of cone $B$? Express your answer as a common fraction. [asy]
size(260);
draw(ellipse((0,0),14.8,6),S);
label("Cone $A$", (0,-6), S);
draw((0,28.3)--(0,0),dashed);
label("$28.3$",(0,14),SW);
draw((-14.8,0)--(0,28.3)--(14.8,0));
draw("$14.8$",(-14.8,0)--(0,0),N,dashed);
draw(ellipse((50,0),28.3,6),S);
label("Cone $B$", (50,-6), S);
draw((21.7,0)--(50,14.8)--(78.3,0));
draw("$14.8$",(50,14.8)--(50,0),W,dashed);
draw("$28.3$", (21.7,0)--(50,0),N,dashed);
[/asy]
答案：\frac{1}{3}
解决方案：The volume of a cone is $V = \frac{1}{3}\pi r^2h$.
So the volume of a cone $A$ is $\frac{1}{3}\pi * 14.8^2 * 28.3 = 6184.756122177123$.
The volume of a cone $B$ is $\frac{1}{3}\pi * 28.3^2 * 14.8 = 28399.54292621613$.
Thus the ratio is $\boxed{\frac{1}{3}}$.

