问题：Find the smallest positive real number $x$ such that
\[\lfloor x^2 \rfloor - x \lfloor x \rfloor = 6.\]
答案：\frac{6}{1}
解决方案：Let $f = \{x\}$. Then, $x = n + f$ where $n = \lfloor x \rfloor$ and $\lfloor f^2 \rfloor = 0$.
This implies that $x = n + f$ and we can replace $x^2$ with $n^2 + 2nf + f^2$.
\begin{align*}
\lfloor x^2 \rfloor - x \lfloor x \rfloor = 6 \\
\lfloor n^2 + 2nf + f^2 \rfloor - (n+f)n = 6 \\
\lfloor 2nf + f^2 \rfloor - fn = 6 \\
\lfloor 2nf + f^2 \rfloor = fn + 6
\end{align*}
Thus we can solve for the fractional part
\begin{align*}
n = \frac{6}{\{x\}} \implies x = \frac{6}{\{x\}} + \{x\} = \frac{6}{\{x\}} + x - \lfloor x \rfloor \\
\lfloor x \rfloor = \frac{6}{\{x\}}
\end{align*}
So the first solution for x is $\boxed{\frac{6}{1}}$.

