$AF = \dfrac{AB \cdot AC \cdot \sin \angle A}{BC}.$
Also, from the angle sum formula for cosine, $\cos(A - B) = \cos A \cos B + \sin A \sin B.$ Since $\angle A - \angle B = 90^o,$ we know that $\cos(A - B) = 0,$ so
