label("$D$", (2.8,2), NE);
label("$E$", (4.8,2), NE);
label("$F$", (5.3,1.05), SE);
label("$G$", (4.3, 1.05), SE);
[/asy]
答案：32
解决方案：The triangles are equilateral, so $AB = AC = BC = 4$, $AD = DE = AC$, $AE = EF = BD$, $GF = EF = BD$.
$DG = AG/2 = 4/2 = 2$, so we can say that $BG = AD - DG = 4 - 2 = 2$.
$FE = AE - AF = AE - DG - AF = AE - DG - (FE - AF) = AE - DG - AE + BD = BD - DG = 2$

The perimeter $ABCDEFG$ is $AB + BC + CD + DE + EF + FG + GA$
Using the above relationships, we can simplify it to $(AB + BD + BC) + (AG + DG + DF + FE) + (CF + EF + FG)$
Since $AG = 2\times CD$, $DF = 2\times FE$, and $CF = 2\times GE$, we can replace these in the equation to get:
$(AB + BD + BC) + 2\times (CD + DF + EF) + 2\times (GE + CF + FG)$
$AB + BD + BC$ is just the perimeter of triangle $ABD$ which is equal to $2\times AC = 8$
$CD + DF + EF$ is just $CD + EF$, which is equal to $AC$. So $2\times (CD + DF + EF) = 2\times AC = 16$
$GE + CF + FG$ is just $GE + FG$, which is equal to $AB$. So $2\times (GE + CF + FG) = 2\times AB = 8$

Therefore, the perimeter of the figure $ABCDEFG$ is $8 + 16 + 8 = \boxed{32}$.

